+           ```tabular

-         column  Anchor
-         column  Written
-         column  Matches
-         row  `Start`  `^` or `\A`  the start of the whole input
-         row  `End`  `$` or `\z`  the end of the whole input
-         row  `WordBoundary`  `\b`  where a word character (`\w`, ASCII) meets a non-word one
-         row  `NonWordBoundary`  `\B`  where it does not
-         row  `LineStart`  `^` under the `m` flag  the start of the input, or just after a newline
-         row  `LineEnd`  `$` under the `m` flag  the end of the input, or just before a newline
